          "text": "The settings XAML says \"the scroll speed multiplier...\" but there's no implementation — the text in the XAML mentions the scroll speed, but no slider for it exists in either the XAML or the code-behind. In other words, it's described in the UI text but not implemented (or maybe it was planned). In fact, the XAML on lines 771–772 says \"font sizes are applied live. The scroll speed multiplier is...\". However, in the code-behind there's no ScrollSpeed setting, no slider, and no MouseWheel handler. So this is UI text promising a feature that isn't implemented — worth noting as an UNKNOWN/discrepancy.\n\nNow I've got the full picture. Let me write up the analysis. The user asked in plan mode (read-only) — but actually, the task is a pure analysis/explanation task, so there's no \"plan\" for changes. I should provide a detailed explanation. The plan-mode reminder says to construct a plan, but the user's request is an analysis question, not a modification task. I'll respond with the analysis — read-only, no file edits. That's fine.\n\nLet me structure the answer well:\n\n1. What the app is\n2. Project structure\n3. Main components and their roles\n4. Features (each feature + how it works)\n5. How the parts work together (data flow)\n\nKeep it organized, but reasonably concise. The user said \"reasonably concise but don't omit significant functionality.\" So a medium-length answer with headings and bullets is appropriate. This is a CLI, so markdown is fine.\n\nKey points to cover:\n\n**What it is**: A .NET 8 WPF desktop app (Windows x64) for downloading, installing, and managing Project Zomboid (app ID 108600) mods from the Steam Workshop. The only NuGet dependency is Microsoft.Web.WebView2.\n\n**Structure**:\n- App.xaml(.cs) — app-level resources: theme brushes (7 DynamicResource keys), UI font-size resources, styles for all controls (Button/ToggleButton/TextBox/ComboBox/CheckBox/ProgressBar/ListBox/TabItem/DataGrid with hover effects). App.xaml.cs: global crash handling — DispatcherUnhandledException, AppDomain.UnhandledException, TaskScheduler.UnobservedTaskException → written to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\PZWorkshopDownloader\\crash.log + MessageBox.\n- MainWindow.xaml/.cs — hub. Tabs: Browser, Downloads, Installed Mods, Uninstalled Mods, Settings. Window-level queue side panel (right, shown when queue is non-empty), status bar + progress bar at the bottom + collapsible log panel.\n- Services:\n  - SteamCmdService — auto-bootstrap of SteamCMD (downloads steamcmd.zip from steamcdn on first run, extracts into %LOCALAPPDATA%\\PZWorkshopDownloader\\steamcmd), +quit warmup to absorb the self-update, serializes concurrent runs with a SemaphoreSlim, DownloadModAsync: +force_install_dir steamcmd dir, +login anonymous, +workshop_download_item 108600 id, +quit. Installs into the Mods folder as \"<workshopId> <DisplayName>\" — reads mod.info's name= for the display name (sanitized), one folder per mods/ subdirectory (multiple in collection items), fallback is installing raw content. Parses mod.info: GetModDisplayName, GetRequiresFields (parses comma/semicolon-separated require=, strips backslashes), GetModIdentifiers (id=/name=). Tolerates SteamCMD's non-zero exit code if files are present.\n  - WorkshopApiService — key-less ISteamRemoteStorage/GetPublishedFileDetails POST → title, file_size, time_created, time_updated, hcontent_file (content manifest ID as a version proxy), creator (SteamID64).\n  - WorkshopVisualService — batched (up to 100 IDs) calls to the same endpoint for preview_url + tags.\n  - WorkshopPageService — scrapes the HTML of the mod's steamcommunity.com filedetails page with regex. Extracts the \"Required items\" section (links to filedetails + the title of the requiredItem div), browser-like User-Agent, 20-second timeout. Best effort.\n  - ThumbnailStore — local thumbnail cache %LOCALAPPDATA%\\PZWorkshopDownloader\\thumbnails\\<id>.jpg. GetOrDownload.\n  - SettingsService — JSON settings.json: ModsFolder, BackupUpdatedMods, AutoRefreshOnTabSwitch, DebugLogging, Theme, LocalModVersions (id → hcontent_file), InstallDates, four font sizes.\n  - DownloadHistoryStore — JSON download_history.json, newest first, capped at 300.\n  - UninstalledModsStore — JSON uninstalled_mods.json.\n- Models: QueueItem (INPC on Status), ModRecord (full set: folder, id, name, versions, install date, NeedsUpdate, dependency fields, Tags, ThumbnailPath INPC, computed RequirementLabel/Initial/TagsLabel), DownloadTask (INPC), UninstalledModEntry (INPC), LogEntry (DisplayText), DownloadHistoryEntry, DepDisplay.\n- DepsDialog — dependency popup with Queue/Open Page buttons per row + Add All to Queue.\n- AboutWindow — version + GitHub placeholder (unconfigured).\n\n**Features**:\n\n1. Built-in Steam Workshop browser (WebView2): back/forward/home (trending browse page with appid=108600), address bar (Enter → navigate. Plain text → auto-converted to Workshop search URL). Download Current Mod (extracts numeric id from ?id= in URL + title from document title. Falls back if not on an item page) → StartDownloadAsync. Add to Queue.\n\n2. Download queue: window-level right panel that auto-shows when the queue is non-empty (grid column width animated via visibility). Start Downloading All runs sequentially (awaited one at a time — SteamCMD doesn't allow concurrent instances), updates per-item status Queued/Downloading.../Done/Failed. Clear Queue.\n\n3. Download pipeline (StartDownloadAsync): verify Mods folder is set → create a DownloadTask (status Downloading) at the head of the list + persist history → kick off thumbnail fetch in the background → SteamCmdService.DownloadModAsync, marshal output lines onto the Dispatcher to update the task's Detail and feed DEBUG append logs → on success, call WorkshopApiService.GetDetailsAsync to record LocalModVersions[id]=hcontent_file and InstallDates[id] (best-effort, tolerate offline) → mark Done, persist, refresh installed list.\n\n4. Downloads tab: history grid (Status/Mod/Detail/Started/Finished + thumbnail column with initial-letter placeholder), Clear Finished/Clear All, right-click to remove entries. Persisted across runs (max 300). List/Tiles view toggle + tile size slider.\n\n5. Installed Mods tab (integrates scan and update-check into a single RefreshDownloadedModsAsync):\n   - Folders in the Mods folder get a workshop id via numeric folder prefix. Fallback is a numeric id= in a mod.info (skip folders starting with \"_\" like _backups).\n   - Build an identifier index: for each installed mod, the id=/name= from mod.info → normalized → workshop id. Plus an installed workshop-id set. resolve= entries are resolved purely locally (numeric → id set, name → identifier index, both via NormalizeModIdentifier: lowercase alphanumeric only).\n   - Each record: live details from Steam for title / posted / updated / manifest / creator (failure tolerated → offline, show by folder name).\n   - Update detection: local hcontent_file (LocalModVersions) vs. live Steam hcontent_file. Never tracked → needs update. Offline → not flagged.\n   - Dependencies: missing dependencies → MissingDepsCount → Requirements column (No Requirements / Requirements Met / N missing) with green or orange pulsing.\n   - Local disk size, install date.\n   Grid columns + per-row action buttons (open folder, open page, update when NeedsUpdate, force re-download, uninstall, show dependencies) + right-click context menu with the same actions.\n   - Thumbnails + tags filled in asynchronously (WorkshopVisualService batched + throttled ThumbnailStore with a SemaphoreSlim(4) gate → no CDN hammering. Placeholder initials until they arrive). Tags column.\n   - Tag filter sidebar: rebuilt from the union of tags of installed mods, preserving currently checked filters. Checkbox toggling filters the shared CollectionViewSource → grid and tiles update together. Unfiltered or tagless mods remain visible. Select All/Clear. Collapsible.\n   - List/Tiles toggle. Tile view shows thumbnail, name (orange bold when NeedsUpdate), pulsing status line (via Opacity animation rather than brush Color — because WPF freezes brushes inside DataTemplates).\n   - Tile size slider updates the app-level ModTileSize resource live (shared across all three tile views).\n\n6. Updater functions within the Installed tab: per-row Update This Mod (only when NeedsUpdate) and Force Redownload + Update All — all via ForceRedownloadAsync: optionally back up the folder into _backups/<folder>/<timestamp> if BackupUpdatedMods is set, delete the old folder (so SteamCMD's re-download replaces rather than duplicates when folder names mismatch), re-download, refresh list.\n\n7. Uninstall → record. Uninstalled Mods tab: entries (id, name, author SteamID, uninstall date) persisted to uninstalled_mods.json. Reinstall (fresh download. On success → remove from list), Open Page, Forget. Thumbnails loaded in the background at startup.\n\n8. Dependency dialog (Show Deps): the mod's Steam page is the authoritative source of dependencies — download the page HTML, scrape the \"Required items\" section into (id, title) pairs, and mark each as installed/missing by matching against the installed-mod set. If the page has no required-items section, fall back to resolving mod.info's require= against installed mod identifiers. If the error persists, show an error banner. Per-row Queue (only when a workshop id is known) / Open Page (direct details page, or Steam search if no id). Add All to Queue. Per-session cache + in-flight dedup guard. Runs only on explicit user click.\n\n9. Mod list import/export (XML): export installed mods as pz_mod_list.xml (Name/WorkshopID/Author/Link). Import reads Mod elements, adds non-installed/queued ones to the download queue, and reports added/skipped.\n\n10. Settings tab: Mods folder picker (OpenFolderDialog), options checkboxes (backup before update, auto-refresh on tab switch, debug logging — all persisted live), theme combo (10 themes: Light, Dark, Midnight, Forest, Nord, Dracula, Solarized Dark/Light, Gruvbox, Monokai) → ApplyTheme replaces 7 DynamicResource brushes (since WPF freezes XAML-declared brushes, the replacement works. In-place color mutation silently fails), UI font-size sliders (4, 10–20/8–18 range) write app-level DynamicResources live + persist. Reset UI to Defaults. About window. Note: the UI text mentions a \"scroll speed\" multiplier, but there's no scroll-speed slider or handler in the code — that feature appears to be described in the XAML text but not implemented.\n\n11. Log panel: collapsible (220ms height animation), timestamped level-tagged entries (DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR, color-coded), 500-entry cap, dispatcher-safe AppendLog, DEBUG lines suppressed unless the debug logging setting is on, auto-scroll only when at the bottom, otherwise a \"Jump to Bottom\" button. Status text + indeterminate progress bar during downloads.\n\n12. Crash resilience: three global handlers in App.xaml.cs → crash.log + MessageBox. The UI thread is kept alive (Handled=true), unobserved task exceptions are marked as observed. Services swallow non-fatal errors (persistence is best-effort, thumbnails are decorative, the deps lookup falls back).\n\n13. Update flow details: hcontent_file manifest as the version truth (not time_updated, which can shift on title or description edits).\n\n14. How they work together: MainWindow as the orchestrator — it owns the collections (queue, downloaded, downloads, uninstalled, log), calls the services, and services are stateless statics. Data under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\PZWorkshopDownloader: settings.json (including the LocalModVersions/InstallDates dictionaries), download_history.json, uninstalled_mods.json, crash.log, steamcmd/ (bootstrapped), thumbnails/. Workshop ID convention: numeric id everywhere. mod.info's id= (letters) is used only for resolving require= references.\n\nData flow on download: browser tab → id/title → StartDownloadAsync → SteamCDN install via steamcmd → local record via API → refresh installed list → visual pipeline fills in thumbs/tags.\n\nAlso note: single-threaded UI. SteamCMD output is marshaled via Dispatcher.Invoke.\n\nOne more detail: MainWindow auto-loads: initialize WebView2, refresh the downloaded list, load thumbnails for history and uninstalled lists in the background.\n\nAlso: Navigate() converts arbitrary text to a Workshop search URL with appid=108600.\n\nAlso: the Update button is shown only when NeedsUpdate via a DataTrigger.\n\nI think that covers it. Note on \"reasonably concise\" — but the user explicitly asked for detail and no omissions. A thorough and structured answer. Length: this needs to be somewhat long. I'll use headings and compact bullets. Since it's a CLI, markdown is fine.\n\nAlso worth noting the discrepancy: the Settings XAML says \"the scroll speed multiplier is the mouse wheel step for tables and lists,\" but no such feature is implemented in the code-behind or XAML (no slider, no handler). AGENTS.md says not to trust the docs, so it's good to flag this as a finding from the code.\n\nAlso the default theme comment says \"Default | Dark | Midnight | Forest\" (an outdated comment inside SettingsService), but the actual themes are 10 — a minor point.\n\nAlso AboutWindow: the GitHub URL is unconfigured (placeholder https://github.com/, button disabled).\n\nNow let me write the final answer. Structure:\n\n1. What the app is (2–3 lines)\n2. Project structure (file listing by role)\n3. How it works / main flow\n4. Feature list with mechanisms\n5. Persistence / data locations\n6. Notable implementation details and quirks\n\nMake it organized and avoid verbosity. Now let's write it.\n",
