          "text": "Now let's implement change 1: Add a \"Reset Steam Command Cache\" button to the Settings tab (with a confirmation dialog). Add the following section under Options:\n\n```xaml\n<StackPanel Orientation=\"Horizontal\" Margin=\"0,0,0,20\">\n    <Button Content=\"Reset Workshop Cache...\" Click=\"ClearSteamCmdCache_Click\"/>\n    <TextBlock ... hint .../>\n</StackPanel>\n```\n\nWhere to add it? After the Options checkboxes section (before the Theme section). Add the button and a small helper text.\n\nCode-behind:\n```csharp\nprivate void ClearSteamCmdCache_Click(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)\n{\n    var contentRoot = SteamCmdService.GetWorkshopContentRoot();\n    if (!Directory.Exists(contentRoot))\n    {\n        MessageBox.Show(\"The SteamCMD workshop content folder does not exist yet, so there is nothing to clear.\", \"...\", ...Info);\n        return;\n    }\n\n    var confirm = MessageBox.Show(\n        \"Clear the cached Workshop downloads?\\n\\n\" +\n        $\"This deletes the contents of:\\n{contentRoot}\\n\" +\n        \"(SteamCMD itself is not touched.)\\n\\nMods already installed into your Mods folder are not affected; \" +\n        \"items will be re-downloaded on next check.\",\n        \"Clear Workshop Cache\", MessageBoxButton.YesNo, MessageBoxImage.Question);\n    if (confirm != MessageBoxResult.Yes) return;\n\n    try\n    {\n        var count = 0;\n        foreach (var dir in Directory.GetDirectories(contentRoot))\n            Directory.Delete(dir, recursive: true);\n        // Should we count the deleted ones? Let's count directories + files\n        ...\n    }\n    catch (Exception ex) { ... }\n}\n```\n\nA better counting method: before deletion, count the number of top-level entries (files + directories). Count `Directory.EnumerateFileSystemEntries(contentRoot)` and delete each entry.\n\nAdd to SteamCmdService:\n```csharp\npublic static string GetWorkshopContentRoot() =>\n    Path.Combine(SteamCmdDir, \"steamapps\", \"workshop