uish directories: use File.Exists(entry).\n\n```csharp\n        foreach (var entry in entries)\n        {\n            if (Directory.Exists(entry)) Directory.Delete(entry, recursive: true);\n            else File.Delete(entry);\n        }\n        return entries.Count;\n    });\n```\n\nAn async lambda returning a count; WrapSteamCmd returns an int. Then:\n\n```csharp\n    if (ok > 0)\n    {\n        AppendLog($\"Cleared {ok} cached Workshop entr{(ok == 1 ? \"y\" : \"ies\")} from SteamCMD content cache.\");\n        StatusText.Text = $\"Cleared {ok} cached item(s).\";\n    }\n    else { MessageBox... \"nothing to clear\"; }\n```\n\nWait — about counting: the entries are the top-level ones. If there's a `108600` directory containing many mod IDs, the count will show as 1. Better UX: count the number of mod folders under the appid directory. But the content root we delete is content\\108600 — actually the user specifically asked about %LOCALAPPDATA%\\PZWorkshopDownloader\\steamcmd\\workshop\\content\\108600\\! Note: they said the path is content\\108600 (appid directory). AGENTS.md says the content cache is at ...\\steamcmd\\steamapps\\workshop\\content\\108600\\<id>\\ — the actual path includes the steamapps\\workshop prefix. The user omitted \"steamapps\" (a slight typo), but intent-wise it's the same thing: the workshop content cache for appid 108600 under the app's steamcmd directory. The actual layout in the code is content/108600/<id>. Let's use GetWorkshopContentRoot() = steamcmd\\steamapps\\workshop\\content\\108600 and delete its child directories (each = one workshop item). Counting: the number of directories under the appid directory = the number of cached items.\n\nImplementation:\n```csharp\nvar ok = await SteamCmdService.WithSteamCmdLockAsync(() =>\n{\n    var roots = Directory.GetDirectories(contentRoot);\n    foreach (var r in roots) Directory.Delete(r, recursive: true);\n    // Also delete stray files directly under the content root? Leave them; keep it simple.\n    return roots.Length;\n});\n```\n\nIn addition, after clearing the cache, the thumbnail cache is separate (thumbnails/) and is unaffected — good, the thumbnails remain.\n\nAfter clearing, should we refresh the installed list? Not needed: installed mods are in the user's Mods folder (a separate location); the SteamCMD cache is only the staging area. However, if the SteamCMD installation itself is missing (the user deleted steamcmd.exe separately), EnsureSteamCmdAsync will re-download it. No problem.\n\nAlso, if nothing exists, show a message.\n\nMessage wording:\n\"CLEAR the SteamCMD Workshop content cache?\\n\\nDeletes {n} cached Workshop item folder(s):\\n<root>\\n\\nSteamCMD itself and its config are not touched, and installed mods in your Mods folder are unaffected.\\n\\nProceed?\"\n\nNext, add a XAML section to the Settings tab. Where? Insert a new \"SteamCMD\" section after the Options checkboxes (before Theme). The settings screen currently has: Mods Folder, Options (3 checkboxes), Theme, UI Customization, Reset UI, About. Insert between Options and Theme:\n\n```xaml\n<TextBlock Text=\"SteamCMD\" Foreground=\"{DynamicResource AccentBlue}\" FontWeight=\"Bold\" Margin=\"0,0,0,10\"/>\n<StackPanel Orientation=\"Horizontal\" Margin=\"0,0,0,24\">\n    <Button Content=\"Clear Workshop Content Cache...\" Click=\"ClearSteamCmdCache_Click\"/>\n    ...\n</StackPanel>\n```\n\nKeep it simple: heading \"SteamCMD\" + a hint TextBlock + button. A StackPanel containing the button and hint text, similar to the Mods Folder layout.\n\nChange 2 — AboutWindow.xaml.cs:\n```csharp\npublic const string GitHubUrl = \"https://github.com/IDRdh7/PZWorkshopDownloader\";\nprivate const bool GitHubConfigured = true;\n```\nDelete/adjust the comment. Keep GitHubNoteText as is; when configured, it displays the default design-time text \"Please consider supporting this...\"? Let me check the About XAML — GitHubNoteText has design-time Text \"No GitHub repository has been configured for this project yet.\" Is the Text set in XAML with x:Name? In AboutWindow.xaml: `<TextBlock x:Name=\"GitHubNoteText\" Text=\"Please consider supporting this project by leaving a star on GitHub.\" .../>`. The constructor overwrites the Text when !GitHubConfigured. When configured = true, the TextBlock keeps the XAML text (with a star hint). And the button gets enabled (by default Enabled, disabled when unconfigured). So with configured=true: button enabled + star note.\n\nUpdate the header comment accordingly.\n\nChange 3 — The tile slider. There are 3 sliders, each inside a per-tab StackPanel (rows: 1). Give each an x:Name: DownloadsTileSizeSlider, InstalledTileSizeSlider, UninstalledTileSizeSlider. Add a Visibility property? The Checked handler sets it. Initial state: List mode is active (List toggle IsChecked=True) → slider should start Collapsed in XAML.\n\nAdd to each Checked handler:\n```csharp\nDownloadsTileSizeSlider.Visibility = tiles ? Visibility.Visible : Visibility.Collapsed;\n```\nNote: the handler early-returns with `if (sender is not ToggleButton tb || tb.IsChecked != true) return;` — that is, it only handles the case where something became checked. The unchecking of the other toggle is done by `DownloadsListToggle.IsChecked = false` inside the handler. So the handler sees exactly one \"check\" event per switch (the one that became checked), so setting the visibility there is sufficient.\n\nAlso add a guard for IsLoaded? These already guard IsLoaded.\n\nOne subtle point: the `IsChecked=\"True\"` in XAML fires the Checked handler during InitializeComponent → the IsLoaded guard filters it out. Good.\n\nAnother subtle point: switching tiles→list: the List toggle's Checked fires → sets the slider to Collapsed. Switching list→tiles: the Tiles toggle's Checked fires → sets it to Visible.\n\nTile size slider XAML: add `Visibility=\"Collapsed\"` and x:Name.\n\nThree places: Downloads (line ~234), Installed (line ~352), Uninstalled (line ~626).\n\nNext, FEATURE_ROADMAP sync: add Batch 5:\n```\n## Batch 5 — Additional fixes and improvements — ✅ DONE (WIP?)\n```\nHmm. Convention: mark checkboxes with [x] as we proceed. Add a new batch section at the end with [x] items:\n- [x] Settings: \"Clear Workshop Content Cache\" button (with confirmation; deletes SteamCMD's cached Workshop item for appid, leaves SteamCMD itself)\n- [x] About dialog: real GitHub repository link (https://github.com/IDRdh7/PZWorkshopDownloader)\n- [x] Tile size slider only shown in Tiles mode (hidden in List mode, all three tabs)\n\nSince all 3 will be completed within this session, they can go in as [x] immediately — matches the \"check items off as we progress\" style. Let's add a Batch 5 section marked DONE.\n\nNow let's execute the edits. Batch 1: edit SteamCmdService + edit MainWindow's XAML + edit code-behind.\n",
